{
  "summary": "Rejects node startup with an initialization error if -port=65535 and the onion service bind port must be derived from it. The node now checks that default_bind_port is below UINT16_MAX before computing the default onion port, while continuing to allow -port=65535 when an explicit onion port is specified or when listening is disabled.",
  "problem": "Bitcoin Core derives the default Tor onion service bind port by adding 1 to -port. When -port is set to 65535, the uint16_t addition wraps to 0, causing the node to bind 127.0.0.1 on an arbitrary OS-assigned ephemeral port and point the automatic Tor onion service there.",
  "evidence": [
    "Commit message and description explain the integer overflow: 'The default onion bind uses -port + 1. With -port=65535 this wraps to 0, so the node binds 127.0.0.1 to a random port and the automatic onion service points there.'"
  ],
